    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d500-a2">

                <pb facs="0787" n="659" xml:id="pg659"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in inclosure in No.
                    21.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Müller to Mr.
                            Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brooklyn, N. Y.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-05-02"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 2,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a sworn narrative of the
                    indignity and outrage put upon me by the Russian Government on a recent visit to
                    Russia armed with a passport of the United States. I ask you respectfully to
                    take such action in the premises as you shall deem proper.</p>
                <p>Any further information desired I will cheerfully furnish if required.</p>
                <p>Yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>I. MÜLLER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
